CHAPTER IV — AUTONOMOUS SQUAD AI
Autonomous Squad AI is the beating heart of Obsidian Protocol.
It transforms squads from passive units into thinking battlefield actors capable of flanking, breaching, suppressing, retreating, coordinating, and adapting to dynamic conditions — all without direct micromanagement.

This chapter defines how squads interpret intent, evaluate risk, choose actions, and coordinate with other units.

4.1 Squad Personalities
Every squad has a personality profile that influences decision‑making. Personalities are lightweight behavioral modifiers layered on top of core AI logic.

Personality Types
Aggressive — prioritizes damage, pushes advantages

Cautious — avoids high‑risk engagements

Methodical — prefers structured formations and firing lines

Adaptive — rapidly changes tactics based on conditions

Recon — prioritizes visibility, stealth, and information

Supportive — focuses on repairs, escorts, and reinforcement

Personality Effects
Personality affects:

Engagement range

Retreat thresholds

Target priority

Formation choice

Breach behavior

Suppression response

Pathfinding aggressiveness

